|ID = 686
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Goddess of Light Sirius
|name2 = Goddess of Sunrise Sirius
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Goddess of Sunrise Sirius''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Goddess of Sunrise Sirius is a very strong backliner against traited enemies, being strong against all traits and also having immunity to most debuffs. Though somewhat expensive, she has a very low CD of 78 seconds and Colossus Slayer.

Sirius has better generalist coverage than most other units in the game, only being ineffective against traitless and metal. She can still somewhat tank waves and surge if it is from a traited enemy. While her Knockback and Warp immunities can be helpful against [[Red EnerG]] and [[Gardeneel Bros.]] respectively, most of the time they will cause Sirius to suffer a damage knockback from enemies with these effects. Lastly, her multi-hit long distance attacks require 2.33 seconds to fully execute, and so might cause Sirius to only deal partial damage to enemies with many knockbacks (which becomes less of a concern the stronger enemies become); they only overlap within a precarious 350-431 range, and their lack of backwards range leaves her with no way to protect herself against Zombies burrowing into her personal space.

With Strong Against applying to every enemy with a trait, her decent to mediocre 52,700 HP and ~5,128 DPS at level 30 become boosted to a far more impressive 131,750 HP and ~9,231 DPS (105,400 HP and ~7,693 DPS without Fruit Treasures). If the enemy is a traited colossus, her Colossus Slayer ability stacks multiplicatively with Strong Against to reach an even more monstrous ~188,214 HP and ~14,770 DPS (~150,571 HP and ~12,308 DPS w/o Fruit Treasures). Due to her immunities, she can be used without reservation against debilitating enemies like [[Henry]], [[Croakley]] or [[Gobble]], as well as preventing her Strong buff from being invalidated by Relic enemies or the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]]. Lastly, all of her multi-hit attacks hit further than she stands - by a mere 1 unit for her first hit and 120 units for her second and third hits - allowing her to strike a crowd of tightly-clustered enemies without relying on them to push forward. All of these features in tandem give Sirius amazing compatibility against the majority of traited and colossus enemies in the game.

